# Pattern Recognition

This problem extends **Contains Duplicate**.

Previously we asked:

```text
Have I seen this number before?
```

Now we ask:

```text
Have I seen this number recently?
```

The word **recently** is the clue.

This introduces the **Sliding Window** mindset.

---

# Why the Previous Solution Fails

Consider

```text
nums =

1 2 3 1

k = 1
```

A HashSet tells us

```
1 exists
```

but not

```
Where?
```

The missing information is the previous index.

Therefore,

we need

```text
Number

↓

Last Index
```

---

# Brute Force Solution

Compare every pair.

If

```text
nums[i] == nums[j]
```

check

```text
|i-j|
```

---

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {

    public boolean containsNearbyDuplicate(int[] nums, int k) {

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {

            for (int j = i + 1; j < nums.length; j++) {

                if (nums[i] == nums[j] &&
                    j - i <= k) {

                    return true;

                }

            }

        }

        return false;
    }
}
```

---

## Complexity

