# Common Mistakes

## Mistake 1

Not updating the index.

Wrong

```java
if (!map.containsKey(num)) {
    map.put(num, i);
}
```

Always store the **latest** occurrence.

---

## Mistake 2

Using absolute difference unnecessarily.

Since we process from left to right,

```text
i

>

previousIndex
```

Therefore

```java
i - previousIndex
```

is sufficient.

---

## Mistake 3

Removing the wrong element in the sliding window.

Correct removal:

```java
window.remove(nums[i - k - 1]);
```

Not

```java
window.remove(nums[i - k]);
```

